 "notes": "Draw order and class-by-class mapping come from the comments in stronghold.c and stronghold_blocks.c. The Java statics (piece list, counters, pending list) are file-scope mutable globals in C too (stronghold.c sh_weights, sh_active, sh_pending...), a GPU-contract hazard. I did not confirm that the sblocks dumps include stronghold starts (the populated-chunk tests may cover them instead). Not gaps (triage 2026-09-25, out/plan/remaining-2026-09-25.md): the chest, spawner and door flags are read only while populating the chunk holding the target block, which already ran before any save. Formerly listed as missing: Reading a stronghold piece's saved NBT (func_143011_b: EntryDoor, Left/Right, Steps, the Crossing flags, Chest, Type, Tall, Source, Mob) has no native counterpart; native rebuilds strongholds from the seed, so a chest or spawner flag set in a saved world is not restored."
